{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/1627","id":5157229158,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ8oa8s8AAAABM2USZg","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1627","diff_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1627.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1627.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1627","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/1627/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/1627/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1627/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/statuses/dbfe21c2bc88d97034c3de8e64e8b490ae54688f","number":1627,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[I17:E03] Delivery Lanes: Each Task Row Carries Its Lane","user":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Overview\n\nTask rows carry a board-wide Lane index in their Work Breakdown table. Dependency and issue-format checks validate the assignment, and the available-work survey admits the requested lane and unlaned units through that same raw-cell source. Joined rows share one index or are all unlaned. Deliver mode carries each request's optional lane through every survey path. The board queue reports each Ready unit's lane from the same task rows while retaining its existing placement decisions; Advance carries that returned report to the user.\n\n## Changes\n\nLane ownership, validation, admission and table operations use the epic task row as their data source.\n\n### Task Table\n\n- **Lane beside joins.**\n  Lane follows Joins and precedes Done, holding a bare decimal index or an empty unlaned cell.\n- **Row population.**\n  Epic population accepts each supplied row index; work-item population describes the component and implementation plan.\n\n### Joined Assignments\n\n- **One lane per unit.**\n  The dependency check reports every joined row and its lane when indices differ or indexed and empty cells mix.\n- **Raw index validation.**\n  The shared reader accepts bare decimal indices and empty cells, reporting markup and prose by task before link stripping.\n\n### Table Operations\n\n- **Preserved row data.**\n  Regression fixtures prove populated and empty Lane values survive normalization, reservation, release, delivery linking and completion ticks.\n- **Active guideline mapping.**\n  Validation metadata names the current guideline headings.\n\n### Delivery Admission\n\n- **Requested lane.**\n  A requested index admits matching and unlaned units; a run without a lane admits unlaned units, retaining their existing order.\n- **Explicit unit reports.**\n  The survey names each unit's lane and preserves holds, blockers and merge evidence across lane requests.\n- **Invalid assignments.**\n  Malformed cells and split joined units receive bounded diagnostics and a nonzero result.\n- **Request-scoped input.**\n  Deliver mode reads the lane afresh from each request, supplies none when absent, and shows lane or unlaned during confirmation.\n- **Every survey path.**\n  Initial, resolved-issue and released-hold surveys all carry the request's optional lane.\n\n### Ready Unit Reports\n\n- **Snapshot-only lanes.**\n  The queue reports each free eligible joined unit's task-table index or unlaned state from supplied issue bodies, including rows with no work-item link.\n- **Existing eligibility.**\n  Shared delivery helpers exclude held, running, delivered and dependency-blocked units; producer outputs retain the queue's snapshot boundary.\n- **Independent placement.**\n  Lane annotations preserve Status and assignee calls, and invalid assignments receive explicit findings.\n\n- **Advance report.**\n  Advance retains the returned Ready-unit lane lines and includes their index or unlaned state in its report.\n\n### Lane Planning\n\n- **Confirmed task assignments.**\n  Plan mode confirms the initiative lane decision and row map, follows the owning Joins rule and passes each optional row index to epic-body population.\n\n### Joined Unit Scope\n\n- **Bounded cross-epic diagnostics.**\n  The dependency check names each out-of-epic Joins entry and returns before whole-epic prerequisite or priority evaluation, retaining same-epic lane and dependency checks.\n\n## References\n\n- **R1.** [#1626](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1626) — the initial lane declaration delivery.\n- **R2.** [#1628](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1628) — the task-table lane contract and component-only work items.\n- **R3.** [#1629](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1629) — shared lane validation, joined-unit consistency and table-operation regression evidence.\n- **R4.** [#1632](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1632) — task-table lane admission and observing survey fixtures.\n- **R5.** [#1633](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1633) — Plan mode lane confirmation and task-table population.\n- **R6.** [#1634](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1634) — Deliver mode request input, survey forwarding and lane confirmation output.\n- **R7.** [#1635](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1635) — bounded diagnostics for joins outside their owning epic.\n- **R8.** [#1637](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1637) — Ready-unit lane reporting from issue snapshots and placement-invariance evidence.\n- **R9.** [#1638](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1638) — Advance-mode Ready-unit lane reporting.\n- **R10.** [Architecture Overview](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-delivery-lanes-review/architecture-overview.md) — measured structure, flows and reading order.\n- **R11.** [Agent Review](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-delivery-lanes-review/agent-review.json) — current exact-head and target review evidence.\n- **R12.** [Criterion Audit](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-05-1627-delivery-lanes-review/criterion-audit.md) — all current criteria, row delivery and validation observations.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T15:48:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T04:59:20Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b8f1cb3b74519068f39f34181bcff3f2fd0cc9c7","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:i17/e03/workspace","ref":"i17/e03/workspace","repo":{"id":1137318642,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ8oa8g","name":"workflow-server","full_name":"m2ux/workflow-server","owner":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followi